# Icarus

This is me flying too close to the sun.

Goal: > 95% MNIST test accuracy raw c


## TODO: major rewrite, what did I learn?

- dont over generalize
- use __restrict__ compiler keyword to improve inlining/vector
- use fixed size struct members ex. max array sizes for model (shape, strides)
- function ptr args minimize compiler inlining?
- parallelize with openmp
- use fixed loops instead of stride incrementor index, easily parallelizable
- reduce # of intermediate tensors, custom optimized functions are better
- use arena allocator for per-training run allocations (intermediate tensors etc..)

